  "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, mu any probability measure, b>=0 and a>0. There exist Markov kernels T,H:E to E and B:E times E to E times E. For every u,T(u) is mu reweighted by exp(-(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2) and normalized by its mu integral. H(u) is the law of X+sqrt(a)*Z with X of law T(u) and independent centered identity-covariance Gaussian Z; sqrt(a) is the standard-deviation scale. For every u,y, B(u,y) is the pushforward by x to (u,x) of T(u) tilted by -norm(x-y)^2/(2a), equivalently of mu tilted by -(c/2)*norm(x-m(u,y))^2, with c=b+a^-1 and m(u,y)=c^-1*(b*u+a^-1*y). Both normalized fiber identities hold everywhere, and B retains the first coordinate u. For every probability nu, B composed with nu compProd H equals nu compProd T as full joint laws: sample u from nu and y from H(u), then apply B, to obtain the joint law of u and x with x drawn from T(u). Furthermore for every probability nu on E, probability P on E times E and Markov L:E times E to E times E, s to KL(L(s),B(s)) is measurable, and KL(L composed with P,nu compProd T)<=KL(P,nu compProd H)+the nonnegative integral of KL(L(s),B(s)) against P. T,H,B are chosen after E,mu,b,a and before nu,P,L; the same choice works simultaneously for all later inputs. No additional moment,density,AC,integrability or finite-KL hypotheses. Kernel measurability belongs to the kernel structure; fiber-KL measurability is an additional conclusion. B is the specified ideal kernel whereas L is arbitrary and need not preserve first coordinate; P need not have first marginal nu. The bound concerns full joint laws, with the integral against P. All KL values, addition, inequality and nonnegative integral are extended nonnegative real-valued with infinity permitted. Under the supplied definition probability KL is infinite if AC or required log-density integrability fails. No finiteness is asserted and infinite RHS is permitted. Only the anonymous packet was read; no compilation or source-fidelity judgment.",
  "source_fidelity_verdict": null
